diff --git a/packages/api/session-controller/README.md b/packages/api/session-controller/README.md
index be3f9a0bf5..c199129047 100644
--- a/packages/api/session-controller/README.md
+++ b/packages/api/session-controller/README.md
@@ -84,6 +84,8 @@ GUI model selection requires the exact provider/model pair in the available cata
 
 A successful `selectModel` response acknowledges the Session-local selection without waiting for the default profile setting to save. Default saves run in the background in submission order; a failure logs a warning and leaves the Session selection intact. New Sessions read the last successfully saved default.
 
+`selectModel({ ..., scope: 'session' })` installs the selection for that Session only: the default is not saved, so other Sessions and new Sessions are unaffected. The selection is the same durable `model/selection` event as the default scope, so it survives resume, drives the next request's provider/model, and produces the usual model-switch notice. The response echoes the applied `scope`. A Session follows the live default only while its log names neither a selection nor a request; once either exists it keeps its own model, and no request returns it to following the default.
+
